{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426918-mega-intelligent-psions","id":1426918,"title":"Mega intelligent... Psions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-01T22:00:20-08:00","id":1426918,"title":"Mega intelligent... Psions?","content":"So a question. Megaintelligence is the nova thing. It's why we get the beeping gadgets that can bring back the dead and/or blow up the planet, making your average hero in the trinity era feel like an R&amp;D troubleshooter. <br /> <br /> But biokenetics have the ability to improve their stats--albeit not to mega-intelligent levels. but could there be a high level mode that might let them do that? Not to the &quot;oh Good Lord&quot; and &quot;A god am I&quot; levels you get with high-quantum Novas, but maybe 1 or 2 dots? It seems like something that woudln't be beyond the range of a highly experienced biokenetic, especially if you keep to the lower levels of mega attributes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T01:59:31-08:00","id":1426932,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a bit controversial, but maybe when you use any power that can increase an attribute to 7 dots, you can use 8 successes to gain 1 dot of Mega Attribute, but lose the 7 dot capacity in the process.<br /> <br /> Or, using the 6dot power you can add 1 dot of Mega Attribute by spending 1 psi, also losing the 7dot capacity. Maybe it would stack, so the maximum dot in mega attribute would be 2, but it would cost a lot of successes.<br /> <br /> I have a problem with that, to be honest, but I don\u2019t know exactly what it is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:12:14-08:00","id":1426936,"title":"","content":"Talents and psiads do have ways of adding Scale to their feats, and they have ways of adding dots to their attributes; and when those things align, you get results that are comparable to low-level Mega-Attributes. It's just that when non-Novas do it, the result is both less powerful and more specialized than when Novas do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:20:25-08:00","id":1426938,"title":"","content":"<i>\u201cWhen using a power from a Mode for which the psion has Fleshcrafter, he may spend an additional Psi point to increase the Scale of one aspect of the power ... by one ...\u201d </i><br /> <br /> Intellect is a factor, as is Might, or Stamina, or Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T03:03:14-08:00","id":1426944,"title":"","content":"Would that make the final Scale 2 for purposes of competing with Mega-Whatever novas? I can't recall what base Scale psi effects are for purposes of power clashes, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T05:54:02-08:00","id":1426959,"title":"","content":"That is the idea. In general all powers from Psions have power scale 1, but you can rise by 1 with the 6th dot power of the mode.<br /> <br /> well, they can deal with larger size and speed scales according to the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T06:39:16-08:00","id":1426964,"title":"","content":"Guess that establishes the point where Novas can laugh off psions, then. (Except the ones with Quantakinesis)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T06:52:58-08:00","id":1426968,"title":"","content":"What would stop bioks incorporating higher scale weapons?<br /> <br /> I will leave by saying Psions in Aeon could have a better definition of scale. Having proxies only getting to scale 2 (in terms of being no-sold by aberrant powers) is a bit low-ball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T06:52:59-08:00","id":1426969,"title":"","content":"There's a reason the Aberrants in the antagonist section aren't given large amounts of Scale. Terats get around 5-7 to spread across all the options, IIRC. Porting a Nova from Aberrant into Aeon is not going to work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T07:43:01-08:00","id":1426982,"title":"","content":"The Scale point makes me imagine a giant VARG and then a biok growing up to the same size and punching it out a la Ant-Man knocking out that space leviathan from the end of Endgame.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T09:01:19-08:00","id":1426989,"title":"","content":"Also, Scale isn't as overwhelming as its 1e equivalent was. Sure, you get to a point where the rules say \u201cthe guy on the lower end of the conflict just loses\u201d; but that's, what, four levels? (Going off memory here; it might be three, but I don't think so.) And if you <i>haven't</i> hit the \u201cI win\u201d threshold, you're still at a disadvantage; but it's a disadvantage that can be overcome with a reasonably large dice pool. Conversely, if you <i>have</i> hit it (and often even if you haven't), that just means that it's time to get creative and come up with some other way to take down the Aberrant. They're not likely to have a massive Scale advantage over you in <i>everything</i>; so find something where they don't, and go after them <i>that</i> way. <br /> <br /> And don't forget biotech. A properly equipped psion can use her gear to apply Scale to her powers, and in that way can go toe to toe with higher-Scale Aberrants. She probably can't build the gear herself, and needs the backing of other psions to get it; but that's part of the psions vs aberrant dynamic: individual psions get clobbered; it takes a team of them to take on an Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T09:19:50-08:00","id":1426992,"title":"","content":"100% agree it takes a team of psions to take down an Aberrant, and fighting smart is the way to go. However, dice pools are a bad way to try to overcome scale. If you're psi 5 or lower, each level of scale difference is equivalent to 6.67 dice. Enhancements are probably a better way, and since TC doesn't put a cap on enhancement like Scion does, you can get some pretty crazy enhancement bonuses. All that does, then is require you to ignore the 3+ scale = I win rule to give psions more even footing without scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T09:38:17-08:00","id":1426993,"title":"","content":"3+ Scale means that if I'm Scale 1, you need to be Scale 4 to get the \u201cI win\u201d; if I can push myself up to Scale 2, you need to be Scale 5. And like I said, you're not likely to be Scale 4 or 5 at everything. <br /> <br /> And in keeping with the theme of TC:\u00c6on, I could also see implementing some sort of \u201cswarm Scale\u201d rule: one fire ant is nothing; a million of them will devour everything in sight. In a similar way, a team of psions might be able to operate on a higher Scale than they can manage individually. <br /> <br /> I don't think the \u201cI win\u201d rule needs to be ignored; just worked around with proper gear, teamwork, and/or some lateral thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T11:17:07-08:00","id":1427006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426918-mega-intelligent-psions?p=1426993#post1426993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3+ Scale means that if I'm Scale 1, you need to be Scale 4 to get the \u201cI win\u201d; if I can push myself up to Scale 2, you need to be Scale 5. And like I said, you're not likely to be Scale 4 or 5 at everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar with what a difference in scale means. Maybe we're talking past each other there, but here's the point I was trying to make. A scale difference of 3 would effectively be 6 enhancement if not for the 3+ rule. It is not terrible difficult to get 6 enhancement in Aeon. Therefore, if you didn't want to force the characters to come up with scale improvements, you can drop the 3+ rule and let them go toe to toe with an antagonist with just the enhancements they have access to. That's probably not for everyone, but it's worked fine in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T12:17:48-08:00","id":1427013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426918-mega-intelligent-psions?p=1426964#post1426964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess that establishes the point where Novas can laugh off psions, then. (Except the ones with Quantakinesis)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:16:22-08:00","id":1427033,"title":"","content":"I posted here once a hose rule for psions getting scale. I removed the rules for Mega Attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Psions and Scale</b><br /> Psions are capable of some limited scale increase in their deeds, as long they can already do things beyond human capacities.<br /> Several powers, particularly the powers dealing with speed and some times size, already grant access to a certain degree of scale, and those powers are not affected by this set of rules.<br /> <br /> <b>The 6-dot Powers and Stacking Scale</b><br /> Any scale gained using the methods described bellow can stack with the gain of scale granted by the 6 dots powers. This is the only way a Psion can stack scale above the described below.<br /> For example, a Psi 6 character when using Flash (Thermokinesis 2) can fire an scale 1 attack with enhancement 6, or a scale 2 attack with enhancement 3, and, using Kinetic Mastery, fire an scale 2 attack with enhancement 6 or a scale 3 attack with enhancement 3.<br /> <br /> <b>Durability</b><br /> Psions have some powers that can be used to resist damage, and those are the ones that need most scale to resist the attacks of Aberrants. A Psion with enough power can reduce the finesse of his armor to make it bulkier.<br /> Kinetic Shield (Perikinesis 1) and Energy Shield (Perikinesis 2) can reduce the Soft armor value by 3 to increase the scale by 1, as long the Soft Armor is not reduced to 0 or less (if the soft armor would be 7 or more, it\u2019s possible to reduce it by 6 and increase the scale by 2).<br /> Chimera (Transmogrify 4), Sheath (Thermokinesis 3) and Reinforce (Augendis 1) armors access to the following tags that can be added once.<br /> Armor Tag<br /> Bulky (1): The armor is particularly heavy, adding +1 to the difficulty of any Athletics test while wearing it, but increasing the Durability scale by 1 against any kind of damage it is effective.<br /> <br /> <b>Power</b><br /> Psions have multiple powers that can be used to cause damage, and those are the ones that need most scale to go thru Aberrants\u2019 armors. A Psion with enough power can reduce the precision of his attacks to increase its brute potency.<br /> Enhancement (Electromanipulation 3), Photonic Power (Photokinesis 3), Flash (Thermokinesis 2), Velocity (Telekinesis 2) and Assault (Algesis 2) can reduce the enhancement by 3 to increase the scale by 1, as long the enhancement is not reduce to to 0 or less (if the enhancements would be 7 or more, it\u2019s possible to reduce it by 6 and increase the scale by 2).<br /> Chimera (Transmogrify 4) weapons gain access to the Heavy tag that, combined with a larger size (from Transmogrify 5), can reach scale 3. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:22:03-08:00","id":1427036,"title":"","content":"There are several powers that let you temporarily grant yourself or others reasonable Physical, Mental, or Social Edges. I take that to mean you can grant pretty much any bonus that sounds even vaguely reasonable and just call it an Edge. The only quibbles are whether the bonus is sufficiently narrow in focus, and how many successes must be spent to grant the hypothetical Edge.<br /> <br /> You want 2 Enhancement to balancing on a wire? Sure, there's probably an Edge to do that.<br /> <br /> You want mental scale when playing chess? Sure, that sounds like the sort of thing an Edge should do.<br /> <br /> Given that the Enhance power explicitly stacks with the Swift Edge (granting Speed Scale 3), I presume using Edge/power combos to boost your Scale by two isn't too unusual. This rules interpretation even makes sense, as it allows sufficiently powerful psions to successfully fight all but the most powerful Aberrants, which is something that happens in continuity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T17:17:04-08:00","id":1427061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426918-mega-intelligent-psions?p=1427013#post1427013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I just may not understand how large Scale differences work when nova powers and psi effects clash- particularly some of the high-level psi powers.<br /> <br /> For example, could an adequately Mega-Intelligent nova create an encryption system of scale 5 that even Alex Cassel couldn't crack using Subquantum Computing (Scale 1)<br /> <br /> And while presumably novas that are functioning at strength scale 5 or have scale 5 attacks could punch through any forcefield General Larssen could make, could a strength scale 4 Nova move an object locked into place with the Scale 1 Subquantum Lock?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T18:35:47-08:00","id":1427079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426918-mega-intelligent-psions?p=1427061#post1427061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, could an adequately Mega-Intelligent nova create an encryption system of scale 5 that even Alex Cassel couldn't crack using Subquantum Computing (Scale 1)</div> </div> </div> </div>Subquantum Computing is at least Scale 2, but yes, it\u2019s possible to create a Quantum computer and it would be a Q-Tech. It\u2019s the same for AIs and other Nova creations, they are unbeatable by any mean, and Subquantum Computing would not be capable of reading this creations because it is charged with quantum, like any high rank Nova ou Q-Tech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while presumably novas that are functioning at strength scale 5 or have scale 5 attacks could punch through any forcefield General Larssen could make, could a strength scale 4 Nova move an object locked into place with the Scale 1 Subquantum Lock? </div> </div> </div>General Larssen Force field can be destroyed by a Power scale 5. What a nova can\u2019t destroy is whatever is protected by the 7th dot power of Larsen, as it lock every atom in the place for the duration, no matter what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T22:29:29-08:00","id":1427104,"title":"","content":"I get that once you get into Q-tech the sky's the limit. I meant ordinary encryption- a mathematical encryption system that would run just fine on normal computers, yet be unhackable by low-scale powers. A puzzle too difficult to solve, basically, despite Subquantum Computing's ability to crack any encryption. <br /> <br /> Basically (and in the case of the Subquantum Lock), does Scale limit the ability of powers, or does it apply outside the normal scale system for purposes of power clashes? <br /> <br /> Does a Scale 4 unstoppable force beat a scale 1 immovable object, basically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T04:15:17-08:00","id":1427554,"title":"","content":"There should be advanced hand-held weapons that gave scale (other than needing the heavy tag). The psi powers should be balanced around the weapons, for gameplay reasons. The game core element is not 'Varg - the rider', or even 'Future Military', but the psionic orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T05:03:47-08:00","id":1427564,"title":"","content":"\u201cSeries 4 Deatomizer; Noisy Cricket.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}